node_modules/
dist/
.env
.env.local
*.log

# Generated episodes. Every run writes its own directory of artifacts here -
# corpus, claims, script, renders. Deliberately NOT committed: it is large,
# it is reproducible from the inputs that ARE committed, and a rejected take
# is not something the history needs to carry forever.
runs/

# LIBRARY.md and library.json are rebuilt from the run directories by
# `foundry library`, and runs/ is ignored - so on any machine but the one that
# made them they would describe runs that are not there. Committing them would
# be committing a list of things nobody else can open.
LIBRARY.md
library.json

# series.json is deliberately NOT ignored either, for a sharper version of the
# same reason. It records which platform series each show publishes into, series
# creation has no create-or-get, and there is no way to look one up by title on
# the ingest credential. Lose it and the next publish makes a SECOND shelf that
# starts again at episode one, while the first keeps every episode already
# published. Nothing about either looks wrong in isolation.

# bibles/ is deliberately NOT ignored, and it is the one generated thing here
# that is committed. A run is reproducible from its inputs; a series bible is
# not - it IS the series' memory, and losing it means every later episode
# contradicts freely with nothing to notice. It is a few kilobytes, it changes
# once per published episode, and a diff on it is the most readable record of
# what a show has established that exists anywhere.

# Scratch audio
*.wav
*.mp3
